      "sourceAnalysis": [
        "The full change makes messages.getFull address-header decoding use parseEncodedAddrHeader and joined reconstructed mailboxes, while other headers keep generic MIME-word decoding. Parsing the encoded source before rebuilding names preserves the comma in a quoted display name. A global comma replacement would corrupt other header meanings. The historical test delta removes unnecessary quotes from simple names and adds required quotes around Hörst, Kenny.",
        "At the accepted pin MAILBOX_HEADERS is centralized in ExtensionMessages.sys.mjs. parseEncodedAddrHeader calls parseEncodedHeaderW and makeMimeAddress for named mailboxes, or returns bare email when requested/no name. convertHeaders retains an array per original header value and maps each value to a mailbox-string list joined inside that value; it does not flatten the outer repeated-header array. Missing content-type is added only when addMissingContentType is true.",
        "Current getFull defaults decrypt/decodeHeaders/decodeContent to true for compatibility. It fetches the requested message, parses/decrypts through MsgHdrProcessor, converts read errors to ExtensionError and removes fake body parts for partial messages. convertMessagePart carries decode choices recursively and returns either headers or rawHeaders; root non-content headers move into an outer message/rfc822 envelope. Later raw mode therefore implements part of the review follow-up idea; the original always-decoded landing is not the entire current API. No claim is made that the proposed authors field/deprecation was implemented.",
        "Read the changed historical test hunks, current encoded-name fixture and current checking caller, including missing891–947 header checks. Expected headers are arrays, but header comparison calls toString on them and normalizes tabs. That comparator checks displayed contents without independently proving the exact array partition/shape. Source establishes the array contract; no runtime or strict-shape test result is claimed.",
        "D224115 explicitly accepts while warning about use in compose fields. Author proposes rawHeaders/helper decoding and explains that outer arrays represent repeated header fields, with commas inside one field retaining header-specific meaning. All four actual inline rows are Done. Bug1921765 and reused full Bug1919244 distinguish the getFull follow-up from the earlier MessageHeader author/recipient fix and record later uplift/testing claims; linked examples and later changes were not independently executed."
